; WASD square movement game for the custom CPU
; Screen: 64x48 pixels (matching the supplied examples).
; R0=X, R1=Y, R2=key, R3/R4=previous X/Y, R5=blitter result, R6=scratch.
; The square stays visible while waiting; only valid movement erases/redraws it.
; Controls: W/A/S/D. White 3x3 square. Jump addresses are absolute ROM cells.

